---
import T from '../layouts/T.astro';
import { volumes, samples, links, MAIN_URL, shopUrl, priceRange, readerPages } from '../data/theseus';
const collection = { handle: 'theseus-the-full-collection', digital: 'theseus-the-full-collection-digital' };
---
<T>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="hero dark">
    <div class="wrap hero-grid">
      <div class="hero-txt">
        <p class="eyebrow">A graphic novel in three volumes · Jordan Holt</p>
        <h1>Theseus</h1>
        <p class="lede">The life of the Ancient Greek hero, taken from the writings of Plutarch and spun into a colorful, fully illustrated coming-of-age adventure, both sincere and humorous.</p>
        <div class="ctas">
          <a href="/read/1/" class="btn flame" data-continue>Start reading</a>
          <a href="#buy" class="btn">Get the books</a>
        </div>
        <ul class="facts">
          <li><b>3</b><span>hardcover volumes</span></li>
          <li><b>12</b><span>chapters</span></li>
          <li><b>488</b><span>pages, complete</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <figure class="hero-art">
        <img src="/images/cover-vol3.jpg" alt="Theseus, Volume Three cover: Theseus holds a torch in the labyrinth" width="1600" height="1600" fetchpriority="high" />
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The story -->
  <section class="band" id="story">
    <div class="wrap story">
      <div class="story-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">The story</p>
        <h2>Not the true story. <em>Thankfully.</em></h2>
      </div>
      <div class="story-copy">
        <p class="lede">Theseus is known in mythology for defeating bandits, killing the Minotaur, and eventually ruling over Athens. The story is a fable, but there’s probably a true story underneath the legend. This isn’t it.</p>
        <p>This is what happens when someone loves Greek mythology very much, studies it in depth along with the culture, language and history of the period, is fascinated by the idea of a true story behind the myth, but is simply not a serious person.</p>
        <p>It’s a lovingly faithful retelling of the myth according to Plutarch, crafted into a coming-of-age story garnished with ample humor and an unusually high number of interfering deities.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="wrap hero2">
      <figure class="frame"><img src="/images/art-vol1.jpg" alt="Theseus with his spear, from the Volume One cover" width="1600" height="1600" loading="lazy" /></figure>
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Our hero</p>
        <h3>A teenager burdened with responsibility. Naturally, he avoids it.</h3>
        <p>Rather than the powerful hero of the myth, this Theseus is neither very strong nor particularly smart. He is swept up in a tide of accidental fortunes, and in the schemes and mischief of a host of bored gods.</p>
        <p>But as he meets vicious bandits, each with their own brand of villainy, and the monsters of myth, he starts down the path toward a better and more capable version of himself, while still leaving room for humor.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The books -->
  <section class="band books-band" id="books">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="head-row">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">The books</p><h2>Three volumes. One hero’s whole life.</h2></div>
        <p class="muted">Each chapter behaves like an independent episode, with its own story, while leading further down the path of the overarching tale.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="vols">
        {volumes.map((v) => (
          <article class="vol">
            <div class="frame cover"><img src={v.cover} alt={`Theseus, ${v.title}`} width={v.coverW} height={v.coverH} loading="lazy" /></div>
            <p class="eyebrow">{v.title} · {v.pages} pages</p>
            <h3>{v.hook}</h3>
            <p>{v.text}</p>
            <p class="muted small">{v.extras}</p>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Myth & comedy -->
  <section class="band dark">
    <div class="wrap tone">
      <blockquote>
        <p>“When you stand before a god of Olympus, it must feel like it.”</p>
      </blockquote>
      <div class="tone-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Myth and comedy</p>
        <p>The series is marked by its merger of mythology and comedy. Humor in the vein of <em>Avatar: The Last Airbender</em> and <em>Futurama</em> is balanced with sincere drama. It isn’t an attempt at subversion; it’s solid storytelling.</p>
        <p>The humor is never held at the expense of stakes, scale, and the wonder of meeting the beauty and strangeness of Greek myth. Along the way Theseus encounters the Immortals of the Greek pantheon, clashing or cooperating with gods and goddesses each given a unique spin in the role they play.</p>
        <p>And there’s a colorful cast of characters, creatures and monsters, which give every chapter its own feel, with surprises and discoveries for those who know their Greek mythology. If you don’t, there’s still humor, growth and soul to be found.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="wrap influences">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">On the shelf beside it</p>
        <p><em>Futurama</em> · P. G. Wodehouse · <em>Avatar: The Last Airbender</em> · <em>The Emperor’s New Groove</em> · <em>The Legend of Zelda</em></p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">And the ancients</p>
        <p>Homer · Ovid · Plutarch · Babrius and Phaedrus · Virgil · Aeschylus · Herodotus</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Pages -->
  <section class="band" id="pages">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="head-row">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">Pages</p><h2>Have a few pages.</h2></div>
        <p class="muted">Written, meticulously hand-drawn and colored by one person. Volume One alone took about a thousand very pleasant hours. Select a page to see it larger.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="samples" data-gal>
        {samples.map((s, i) => (
          <button class="frame sample" data-i={i} aria-label={`Enlarge ${s.alt}`}><img src={s.src} alt={s.alt} width={s.w} height={s.h} loading="lazy" /></button>
        ))}
      </div>
      <div class="read-cta">
        <div>
          <h3>Read the first chapter here, free.</h3>
          <p class="muted">Page by page, the way it was drawn. {readerPages.length} pages online so far, with more to come.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="ctas">
          <a href="/read/1/" class="btn flame" data-continue>Start reading</a>
          <a href={links.webtoon} target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn">Read on Webtoon ↗</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Buy -->
  <section class="band buy" id="buy">
    <div class="wrap buy-grid">
      <div class="buy-imgs">
        <figure class="frame"><img src="/images/slipcase-front.jpg" alt="The full collection: three hardcovers in a slipcase" width="1600" height="1600" loading="lazy" /></figure>
        <figure class="frame"><img src="/images/slipcase-back.jpg" alt="The slipcase, reverse" width="1600" height="1600" loading="lazy" /></figure>
      </div>
      <div class="buy-txt">
        <p class="eyebrow">The full collection</p>
        <h2>All of Theseus, in one slipcase.</h2>
        <p>All three hardcover volumes, sewn-bound, in a rigid slipcase adorned with Theseus artwork. Nearly 500 full-color pages, complete. Available signed or unsigned, with free shipping in the US.</p>
        <ul class="options">
          <li><a href={shopUrl(collection.handle)}><span><b>The full collection</b><small>Three hardcovers in a slipcase</small></span><span class="price">{priceRange(collection.handle)}</span></a></li>
          <li><a href={shopUrl('theseus-vol-3-hardcover')}><span><b>Volume Three only</b><small>For those finishing the set</small></span><span class="price">{priceRange('theseus-vol-3-hardcover')}</span></a></li>
          <li><a href={shopUrl(collection.digital)}><span><b>Digital collection</b><small>PDF of all three volumes</small></span><span class="price">{priceRange(collection.digital)}</span></a></li>
        </ul>
        <p class="muted small">Checkout through Carthage Workshop, Jordan Holt’s shop.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Who it's for -->
  <section class="band for">
    <div class="wrap for-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Who it’s for</p>
        <h2>For anyone who loves Greek myth and doesn’t take themselves too seriously.</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>And for those who enjoy endless humor, a good (or bad) pun, and share the philosophy that there’s no such thing as a plot hole, just an opportunity for a joke.</p>
        <p><b>Is it for kids?</b> It reads beautifully with readers 10 and up, and Volume Three is rated 12+. Younger readers may not catch every word of the vocabulary. Comics and Greek mythology were two of the things I loved most as a kid, so if you pick up a copy for a young reader, that makes me very happy.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Creator -->
  <section class="band dark" id="creator">
    <div class="wrap creator">
      <figure class="frame"><img src="/images/sample-2.jpg" alt="Page from Volume Three: “Aegeus? Come inside.”" width="679" height="1050" loading="lazy" /></figure>
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">The creator</p>
        <h2>Jordan Holt</h2>
        <p class="lede">I draw primarily historical, mythological, religious and literary works. I publish my own and work with other publishers.</p>
        <p>I’ve worked in media, advertising and commercial illustration, and have held a faculty position at a university for over ten years. In 2020, at the start of the pandemic lockdown, I launched into my own comic work with Theseus. Six years later, it’s complete.</p>
        <p>Theseus is published by Carthage, my little company. It’s just me and the help my wife generously gives: truly an indie operation. Every page is written, hand-drawn and colored by me. I don’t use AI in any form.</p>
        <p>Next up is <em>PetraCor</em>, an Anglo-Saxon penance fable.</p>
        <div class="ctas">
          <a href={MAIN_URL} class="btn">See all my work ↗</a>
          <a href={links.substack} target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn">Join the newsletter ↗</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="lb" data-lb hidden role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-label="Page viewer">
    <button class="lb-x" data-x>Close ✕</button>
    <button class="lb-nav prev" data-p aria-label="Previous page">‹</button>
    <img data-img alt="" />
    <button class="lb-nav next" data-n aria-label="Next page">›</button>
  </div>
  <script type="application/json" data-samples set:html={JSON.stringify(samples)} />
</T>

<style>
  .hero { padding-block: clamp(48px, 7vw, 104px); overflow: hidden; }
  .hero-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.05fr; gap: clamp(32px, 6vw, 96px); align-items: center; }
  .hero h1 { font: 500 clamp(3.4rem, 7.4vw, 7.4rem)/.9 var(--serif); letter-spacing: .1em; margin: 18px -.1em 26px -.04em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--gold); white-space: nowrap; }
  .hero .lede { max-width: 30ch; color: var(--on-night); }
  .ctas { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px; margin-top: 32px; }
  .facts { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 44px 0 0; display: flex; gap: clamp(20px, 4vw, 48px); border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.14); padding-top: 22px; }
  .facts li { display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
  .facts b { font: 500 2.2rem/1 var(--serif); color: var(--on-night); font-variant-numeric: lining-nums; }
  .facts span { font-size: 12px; letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--on-night-muted); margin-top: 6px; }
  .hero-art { margin: 0; aspect-ratio: 1; box-shadow: 0 30px 80px rgba(0,0,0,.45); }
  .hero-art img { width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; }

  .story { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.5fr; gap: clamp(28px, 6vw, 96px); }
  .story-head h2 { margin-top: 14px; }
  .story-head em { color: var(--flame); }
  .story-copy { max-width: 62ch; }
  .story-copy p:not(.lede) { font-size: 1.05rem; }
  .hero2 { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.1fr 1fr; gap: clamp(28px, 6vw, 96px); align-items: center; margin-top: clamp(64px, 9vw, 120px); }
  .hero2 .frame { aspect-ratio: 1; }
  .hero2 h3 { font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3vw, 2.6rem); margin: 14px 0 20px; }
  .hero2 p:not(.eyebrow) { font-size: 1.05rem; max-width: 52ch; }

  .books-band { background: var(--parch); }
  .head-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.3fr 1fr; gap: 24px 64px; align-items: end; margin-bottom: clamp(36px, 5vw, 64px); }
  .head-row h2 { margin-top: 14px; }
  .head-row p.muted { margin: 0; max-width: 46ch; }
  .vols { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: clamp(20px, 3vw, 44px); }
  .vol .cover { aspect-ratio: 3 / 4; margin-bottom: 20px; box-shadow: 0 14px 40px rgba(36, 26, 44, .18); }
  .vol h3 { font-size: 1.75rem; margin: 10px 0 12px; }
  .small { font-size: 13.5px; }

  .tone { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.2fr; gap: clamp(28px, 6vw, 96px); align-items: start; }
  blockquote { margin: 0; }
  blockquote p { font: italic 400 clamp(2rem, 4.2vw, 3.6rem)/1.15 var(--serif); color: var(--gold); }
  .tone-copy p:not(.eyebrow) { font-size: 1.05rem; }
  .tone-copy .eyebrow { margin-bottom: 18px; }
  .influences { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 32px; margin-top: clamp(48px, 6vw, 80px); padding-top: 28px; border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.14); }
  .influences p:not(.eyebrow) { font: 400 1.3rem/1.5 var(--serif); margin-top: 10px; }

  .samples { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(6, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: clamp(10px, 1.6vw, 20px); }
  .sample { aspect-ratio: 11 / 16; cursor: zoom-in; }
  .sample img { transition: transform .8s var(--ease); }
  .sample:hover img { transform: scale(1.03); }
  .read-cta { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 24px; margin-top: clamp(40px, 5vw, 64px); padding: clamp(24px, 3vw, 40px); background: var(--night); color: var(--on-night); }
  .read-cta h3 { font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 2.6vw, 2.2rem); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .read-cta p { margin: 0; color: var(--on-night-muted); }
  .read-cta .ctas { margin: 0; }

  .buy { background: var(--parch); }
  .buy-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.1fr 1fr; gap: clamp(28px, 6vw, 96px); align-items: center; }
  .buy-imgs { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 14px; }
  .buy-imgs figure { margin: 0; aspect-ratio: 4 / 5; background: #0d0b0f; }
  .buy-txt h2 { margin: 14px 0 18px; }
  .options { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 28px 0 14px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .options a { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; gap: 16px; padding: 16px 4px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); transition: background .2s, padding .2s; }
  .options a:hover { background: var(--paper); padding-inline: 12px; }
  .options b { display: block; font: 500 1.35rem/1.2 var(--serif); }
  .options small { color: var(--muted); font-size: 13px; }
  .price { font: 500 1.2rem/1 var(--serif); white-space: nowrap; color: var(--flame); }

  .for-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: clamp(28px, 6vw, 96px); }
  .for-grid h2 { margin-top: 14px; font-size: clamp(2rem, 3.4vw, 2.9rem); }
  .for-grid p:not(.eyebrow) { font-size: 1.05rem; }

  .creator { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(220px, .8fr) 1.4fr; gap: clamp(28px, 6vw, 96px); align-items: center; }
  .creator .frame { aspect-ratio: 2 / 3; }
  .creator h2 { margin: 14px 0 18px; }
  .creator .lede { color: var(--on-night); max-width: 38ch; margin-bottom: 22px; }
  .creator p:not(.eyebrow):not(.lede) { max-width: 60ch; }

  .lb { position: fixed; inset: 0; z-index: 200; background: rgba(20, 15, 24, .96); display: grid; grid-template-columns: 64px 1fr 64px; align-items: center; justify-items: center; padding: max(56px, env(safe-area-inset-top)) 0 24px; }
  .lb img { max-height: calc(100dvh - 96px); max-width: 100%; width: auto; object-fit: contain; }
  .lb-x { position: absolute; top: calc(16px + env(safe-area-inset-top, 0px)); right: max(20px, env(safe-area-inset-right, 0px)); color: var(--on-night); font: 400 12px/1 var(--sans); letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .lb-nav { color: var(--on-night); font-size: 44px; height: 100%; width: 100%; }

  @media (max-width: 960px) {
    .hero-grid, .story, .hero2, .head-row, .tone, .buy-grid, .for-grid, .creator { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .hero-art { order: -1; max-width: 520px; }
    .vols { grid-template-columns: 1fr; max-width: 560px; }
    .vol .cover { aspect-ratio: 4 / 3; }
    .samples { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
    .creator .frame { max-width: 360px; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .facts b { font-size: 1.8rem; }
    .influences { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .samples { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
    .lb { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .lb-nav { position: absolute; bottom: 12px; width: 56px; height: 56px; } .prev { left: 8px; } .next { right: 8px; }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Sample-page lightbox
  const data = JSON.parse(document.querySelector('[data-samples]')!.textContent!);
  const lb = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-lb]')!, img = lb.querySelector<HTMLImageElement>('[data-img]')!;
  let cur = 0;
  const show = (i: number) => { cur = (i + data.length) % data.length; img.src = data[cur].src; img.alt = data[cur].alt; };
  const close = () => { lb.hidden = true; document.body.style.overflow = ''; };
  document.querySelector('[data-gal]')!.addEventListener('click', (e) => { const b = (e.target as HTMLElement).closest<HTMLElement>('[data-i]'); if (!b) return; show(+b.dataset.i!); lb.hidden = false; document.body.style.overflow = 'hidden'; });
  lb.querySelector('[data-x]')!.addEventListener('click', close);
  lb.querySelector('[data-p]')!.addEventListener('click', () => show(cur - 1));
  lb.querySelector('[data-n]')!.addEventListener('click', () => show(cur + 1));
  lb.addEventListener('click', (e) => { if (e.target === lb) close(); });
  addEventListener('keydown', (e) => { if (lb.hidden) return; if (e.key === 'Escape') close(); if (e.key === 'ArrowLeft') show(cur - 1); if (e.key === 'ArrowRight') show(cur + 1); });

  // "Continue reading" when the visitor has read before
  try {
    const last = Number(localStorage.getItem('theseus-last-page'));
    if (last > 1) document.querySelectorAll<HTMLAnchorElement>('[data-continue]').forEach((a) => { a.href = `/read/${last}/`; a.textContent = `Continue · page ${last}`; });
  } catch {}
</script>
